---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Credits" description="The open-source work Chaalwise is built on.">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Credits</h1>
    <p>
      Chaalwise is free software under the <a href="https://github.com/urbanmorph/chaalwise/blob/main/LICENSE">GNU AGPL-3.0</a>. It is built on the work of
      others, with thanks.
    </p>
    <h2>Chess</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The board is <a href="https://github.com/lichess-org/chessground">chessground</a>, and the rules are{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/niklasf/chessops">chessops</a>, both open-source projects from the <a href="https://lichess.org/">Lichess</a> community,
        under GPL-3.0. Chaalwise is an independent project, not part of or endorsed by Lichess.
      </li>
      <li>The pieces are Colin M.L. Burnett's set, under GPL-2.0-or-later, as distributed with chessground.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Learning</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Spaced repetition uses <a href="https://github.com/open-spaced-repetition/ts-fsrs">ts-fsrs</a> (MIT), the Free Spaced Repetition Scheduler.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Built by</h2>
    <p>
      Chaalwise is made by <a href="https://www.urbanmorph.com/">urbanmorph</a>, led by Sathya Sankaran. The{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/urbanmorph/chaalwise">source is on GitHub</a>; drop a star if you find it useful. How it follows the principles of public
      digital goods is in its <a href="https://github.com/urbanmorph/chaalwise/blob/main/PDGI.md">PDGI scorecard</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Built with</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Astro, Svelte and idb (MIT).</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose ul {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }
  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.6em;
  }
</style>
